Two different issues.

1) The larger the pile of items, the greater the chance of golems.
Stacking vs unstacking affects this slightly (stacked items are more
likely to "shudder", and IIRC shuddering triggers the golem-creation
check), but a large pile of unstacked items is still likely to lead to
golems.

2) Polymorphing items in stacks gives an increased risk of shuddering
and a chance of causing the stacked items to merge into a single item
(the probability goes up as the stack becomes larger), so naming to
make small stacks or single items will slow down polyfodder loss and
get you more loot in the long run.


